    "notes": {
      "item": "Townsend's order for the general-in-chief, quoted in full and attributed (OR II-1 p. 760). It fires only while Scott holds us_general_in_chief and Mansfield serves. Text only, no effects. Lincoln's 16 July question is not in it (B9, Q5).",
      "en|situation.townsend_fugitive_order.text|\\bslaves\\b": "Q9: 'fugitive slaves' is the order's own phrase, inside the quotation and never the narrator's.",
      "en|situation.townsend_fugitive_order.text|\\bservants?\\b": "Q9: 'servants' is the order's word for enslaved people brought with the regiments, inside the quotation, and its context makes that plain."
